# Youth Timer semantic test — runs against the real headless runtime.
#
# Gate C-1 removed the manual `Advance` commands, so nothing in this
# application advances time any more. This exercises what remains real:
# the mode machine, bounded configuration, durable persistence across a
# restart, and the keyboard-shortcut path. Gate C-2 restores elapsing by
# arming a host schedule and reacting to an autonomous ScheduleElapsed
# delivery; the countdown assertions here will move to virtual-clock
# advancement at that point.
#
# NOTE on `activate <name>`: it is direct semantic injection, not simulated
# user interaction. It bypasses host interaction policy entirely -- enabled-
# button filtering, focus, and shortcut resolution -- and can target a node
# whose button is presented disabled. `key <k>` is the command that actually
# passes through that policy. See ../FINDINGS.md, TIMER-F010.

mount
expect text countdown "00:00"
expect text mode "Mode: idle"
expect text sessions "Sessions: 0"
expect text notice ""
expect focus none

# Configure a five-minute session. The display reflects the configured
# duration; with no tick source it does not move on its own.
activate add-1m
activate add-1m
activate add-1m
activate add-1m
activate add-1m
expect text countdown "05:00"
expect text mode "Mode: idle"

# Start via its keyboard shortcut (Enter), not a direct activation, to
# prove the declared Shortcut::Enter reaches the guest as the same
# "start" command.
key enter
expect text mode "Mode: running"

# Configuration is fixed once running.
activate add-1m
expect text countdown "05:00"

# Pause and resume are state-gated.
activate pause
expect text mode "Mode: paused"
activate resume
expect text mode "Mode: running"

# Durable state survives a restart: mode and configuration are the
# canonical model, and the display is always derived from it.
restart
expect text mode "Mode: running"
expect text countdown "05:00"
expect text sessions "Sessions: 0"

# Cancel returns to idle at the configured duration.
activate cancel
expect text mode "Mode: idle"
expect text countdown "05:00"

# A freshly created record is already v2, so no recovery notice appears.
expect text notice ""
